Actually I would keep this open since it seems that changes to opencode are also required. I tried adding this to my `opencode.json`:

```
  "provider": {
    "github-copilot": {
      "models": {
        "claude-opus-4.6-fast": {
          "id": "claude-opus-4.6-fast",
          "name": "Claude Opus 4.6 (fast mode)",
          "family": "claude-opus",
          "attachment": true,
          "reasoning": true,
          "tool_call": true,
          "temperature": true,
          "release_date": "2026-02-07",
          "limit": {
            "context": 200000,
            "output": 64000
          }
        }
      }
    }
```

The model appeared in the list but the server keeps responding with "The requested model is not supported".
